      "quirks": [
        "Feliciana Parish split into East and West Feliciana Parish in 1824 — a GEOGRAPHIC split, not a temporal one. Which successor parish holds a given record depends on exactly where within the old, undivided parish the event occurred, and that is often not known. Records could be under either East or West Feliciana Parish; search both unless a specific residence within the old parish is pinned down.",
        "Both East and West Feliciana Parish marriage registers from 1824 onward are indexed on FamilySearch and full-text searchable."
      ],
      "guide_markdown": "# Locality Guide: Feliciana Parish / East and West Feliciana Parish, Louisiana (1810-1835)\n\nFeliciana Parish split into East and West Feliciana Parish in 1824. This is a geographic split: which successor parish holds a given record depends on where within the old parish the event occurred, and that is frequently unknown. Records for a family resident in the old parish before 1824 may be found under either successor's name after that date — search both.",
